    <tags>cycleswipes touchpad gestures virtual-desktops windows11 tray</tags>
    <summary>Wrap-around four-finger touchpad swipes between Windows 11 virtual desktops.</summary>
    <description><![CDATA[CycleSwipes makes the four-finger touchpad swipe between Windows 11 virtual desktops wrap around:
on the last desktop, swiping "forward" opens the first one; on the first desktop, swiping "back" opens the last one.
On the other desktops Windows switches as usual, and system gestures stay untouched.

It runs in the tray. Start it from the Start menu ("CycleSwipes") and turn on "Start with Windows" in the tray menu.

### Requirements
- Windows 11 (x64) with a Precision Touchpad.
- The four-finger gesture set to "Switch desktops and show desktop" in the touchpad settings.

### Notes
- Over windows running as administrator, use "Restart as administrator" from the tray menu: Windows does not
  deliver touchpad input to standard apps while such a window is in the foreground.
- Wrapping uses VirtualDesktopAccessor.dll (MIT, bundled), which is tied to the Windows build. If it does not
  support your build, the app disables wrapping and shows a notification.
]]></description>
    <releaseNotes>https://github.com/Rexqwer911/cycle-swipes-win11/releases/tag/v{{VERSION}}</releaseNotes>
